inline constexpr std::array<MGTextOverride, 143> kMG2OriginalScript =
{ {
    { 3, 0, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nFight when it's time to fight. Take down those you must take down. \\wCampbell\\r: \nThat's basic - on the battlefield, and in a shooting game.\n...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 2, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nIt's a tap code. They were used to communicate in the Hanoi Hilton, a North Vietnamese prison camp. \\wCampbell\\r: \nBefore that, they were used during the Korean War. Instructions on deciphering the code should be written in the software \\wCampbell\\r: \nmanual...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 3, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nPut yourself in the enemy's shoes. Imagine you're the enemy commander in charge of guarding that area, or a game designer. \\wCampbell\\r: \nYou'll begin to see things you couldn't see before...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 4, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nPlan on the assumption that you won't be able to get supplies...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 8, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nThe enemy mainly detects you by sight, followed by sound. \\wCampbell\\r: \nSound travels about 340 meters per second at room temperature. If the wind is right, it can travel enormous distances. \\wCampbell\\r: \nThe key is to operate silently. If you make a noise, get ready for a fight immediately...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 10, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nTo make your footsteps quieter, plant your heel first and slowly lower your foot toward the joint of your big toe. \\wCampbell\\r: \nThat will silence your footsteps completely... What, you can't do it? ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 14, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nIf you need to know anything about mercenaries or enemy weapons, ask George Kasler - an ex-mercenary turned information \\wCampbell\\r: \nbroker. There's nothing he doesn't know. \\wCampbell\\r: \nHe used to work for us as a military adviser. You can trust him. His frequency is 140.93. \\wCampbell\\r: \nWe'll pick up the tab for the info... just don't ask him about whale cuisine restaurants...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 17, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nListen to his footsteps. Use them to figure out where he is. There are four types of floors in there, and four kinds of footstep sounds. \\wCampbell\\r: \nWhen the enemy fires, aim for the muzzle blast. He'll be right beyond the burst...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 18, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nWIS, OHIO... Maybe WIS is short for Wisconsin. And OHIO is Ohio... \\wCampbell\\r: \nNames of US states. But I thought Dr. Marv had never been to the US... \\wCampbell\\r: \nMaster Miller might know something about it...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 22, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nYou cannot use the radar in areas with high density of Minovsky particles. Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 24, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nYou're good with a cardboard box, right? Why not try posing as part of the cargo? \\wCampbell\\r: \nI'm changing the frequency for our future communications. \\wCampbell\\r: \nYou'll find the new frequency in a photo in the software manual...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 26, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nNatasha's brooch seems to be made out of a shape-memory alloy. Try changing the temperature of the brooch...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 32, "en", "Snake\\s: \nThis is Snake... I've reached the infiltration point. \\wCampbell\\r: \nSnake... Right on time, as always. \\wCampbell\\r: \nLet's get started... Commencing Operation Intrude F014. \\wCampbell\\r: \nLet's go over this one more time. Your mission is to infiltrate Zanzibar Land and rescue the kidnapped Czech biologist, Kio Marv. \\wCampbell\\r: \nSnake, we've provided you with a new piece of equipment - a motion sensor. Try switching it on. \\wSnake\\s: \nRoger... OK, it's on. \\e\\wCampbell\\r: \nThe white dots on your radar are the enemy. The red dot is your current position. \\wCampbell\\r: \nThe radar is equipped with several other types of sensors as well. They should warn you of any unseen dangers. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nWhat's the radar's effective range? \\wCampbell\\r: \nTake a look at your radar display. It shows a 9-screen area centered on your position. However, it may not work in small, enclosed spaces. \\wCampbell\\r: \nIf the enemy spots you, you won't be able to use the radar. Minovsky particles are used to disrupt the enemy, and they interfere  \\wCampbell\\r: \nwith your radar too. \\wSnake\\s: \nGot it. ...Where can I find Dr. Marv? \\wCampbell\\r: \nWell... Dr. Marv has a transmitter implanted in one of his molar teeth. \\wCampbell\\r: \nWhen you get close to him, he'll show up as a red dot on your radar. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nSo I just have to keep an eye out for the red dot... \\wCampbell\\r: \nSnake, use frequency 140.85 for all future communications with me. \\wCampbell\\r: \n...Good luck.\n...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 3, 33, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nI'm changing the frequency for our future communications. \\wCampbell\\r: \nYou'll find the new frequency in a photo in the software manual...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 4, 0, "en", "\\r\\1\nIt's me. One of your fans.\nYou can only jump from there when the wind's blowing north. \\w\\r\\1\nIt usually blows south, but sometimes it changes, just for an instant. \\w\\r\\2\nThat's your chance. Don't miss it. \n...Good luck. \\w" },
    { 4, 1, "en", "\\r\\2\nYou should be able to get card 9 from Predator! \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nDon't you mean card 8? He only had card 8. \\w\\r\\2\nNo, he was in charge of cards 8 AND 9. \\w\\r\\2\nHe must have dropped it somewhere. Check the area he was in! The card should be there.\n...Good luck. \\w" },
    { 4, 2, "en", "\\r\\1\nSnake! Watch out! You're in a minefield! \\wSnake\\s: \nWho are you? \\w\\r\\2\nOne of your fans.\n...Good luck. \\w" },
    { 4, 3, "en", "\\r\\2\nIt's me... One of your fans.\nSnake, watch yourself. \\w\\r\\2\nYou've got company - Night Sight, a surviving member of the Whispers... You know, the legendary guerilla unit. \\wSnake\\s: \nNight Sight... \\w\\r\\2\nHe's wearing a state-of-the-art camouflage suit that makes him practically invisible. \\w\\r\\2\nNot only that, he'll come at you with a gun that makes no sound at all - a wusheng shouqiang. \\w\\r\\2\nNo one has ever laid eyes on him. You understand what that means...? \\wSnake\\s: \nI'm honored to have such a considerate fan. \\w\\r\\2\nUse your ears, Snake!\n...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 4, 4, "en", "Snake\\s\\1: \nThis is Snake. Come in, Charlie. \\wPilot\\r\\1: \nThis is Charlie. Go ahead, Snake... \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nI've got the cartridge. I'm ready to return to base. Making my way to the rendezvous point now! \\wPilot\\r\\1: \nRoger that. I'll meet you there. ...Any passengers? \\wSnake\\s\\1: \n...Just one. A beautiful blonde. \\wPilot\\r: \nI'm looking forward to it...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 4, 5, "en", "Snake\\s\\1: \nWhat's taking you so long? Christmas will be over! \\wPilot\\r: \nThis is Charlie. I'm 10 kilometers from the rendezvous point. \\wPilot\\r: \nHold tight a little bit longer!\nOver and out... \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nHurry!! \\w" },
    { 4, 6, "en", "Snake\\s: \nCharlie... you're late! \\WPilot\\r: \nI thought it would be rude to interrupt you two. \\W" },
    { 5, 0, "en", "Holly\\r: \nI'm Holly. Holly White. \\wHolly\\r: \nI infiltrated Zanzibar Land a month ago, as a journalist. \\wHolly\\r: \nSo I know pretty much how things work around here... I'll help you any way I can. \\wHolly\\r: \nMy frequency is 140.15. Call me... Later! \\w" },
    { 5, 6, "en", "Holly\\r: \nThis isn't a good time! Call me later. Sorry! \\w" },
    { 5, 9, "en", "Holly\\r\\1: \\B19\nSnake! I'm in trouble! They discovered my identity and now I'm a prisoner! Help me! \\wHolly\\r\\1: \nJust when I finally managed to contact Dr. Marv... \\wSnake\\s: \nWhere are you?! Give me your location! \\wHolly\\r: \n...I don't know. I was blindfolded. I think it's somewhere in the tower building... Oh yeah! \\wHolly\\r: \nSnake! ... I hear noises! Off to the left... I hear an elevator! \\wHolly\\r: \nAnd to the right... I hear a noise like a pump. There's water flowing in front of and behind me. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nWater in front and behind... a pump to the right... an elevator to the left? That gives me a sound map. \\wHolly\\r\\1: \nSnake, I don't think they know about my radio yet. But come quick! I'll be waiting. \\w\n\\B-1" },
    { 5, 10, "en", "Holly\\r: \nSnake! ... I hear noises! Off to the left... I hear an elevator! \\wHolly\\r: \nAnd to the right... I hear a noise like a pump. There's water flowing in front of and behind me. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nWater in front and behind... a pump to the right... an elevator to the left? That gives me a sound map. \\wHolly\\r\\1: \nSnake, I don't think they know about my radio yet. But come quick! I'll be waiting. \\w" },
    { 5, 11, "en", "Holly\\r: \nThe tower building is 600 meters tall. There is B1, then floors 1, 10, 20, 30, and the roof on 40F [R]. \\wHolly\\r: \nThere's a north facing veranda on the 20th floor...See ya. \\w" },
    { 5, 13, "en", "Holly\\r: \nThere are three elevators in the tower building. The north elevator stops at floors B1, 1, and 10. \\wHolly\\r: \nThe central elevator stops at floors 1 and 20. The south elevator stops at floors 1 and 30...See ya. \\w" },
    { 5, 14, "en", "Holly\\r: \nI'm pretty sure there's a spiral staircase between floors 10 and 20. It's a bit of a climb, but it'll give you some exercise...See \\wHolly\\r: \nya. \\w" },
    { 5, 18, "en", "Holly\\r: \nEven I don't know what it's like inside the prison. Sorry! ...See ya. \\w" },
    { 5, 20, "en", "Holly\\r: \nIt's not in the blueprints, but... \\wHolly\\r: \nThe kids here say the Zanzibar building and the tower building are connected underground...See ya. \\w" },
    { 5, 24, "en", "Holly\\r: \nThe door to the roof has been sealed shut to keep intruders out. \\wHolly\\r: \nBut it's jury-rigged, so you can probably blow it up pretty easily with plastic explosives...See ya. \\w" },
    { 5, 26, "en", "Holly\\r\\1: \nSnake! You're in danger!! \\wSnake\\s: \nHolly! What's wrong? \\wHolly\\r: \nSnake, it's Madnar... I thought there was something strange about him, so I had the Agency check him out. \\wHolly\\r: \nAfter he was rescued from Outer Heaven... apparently things didn't go well for him. \\wHolly\\r: \nHis radical theories were rejected in the West. \\wHolly\\r: \nHe was dismissed as a madman and shut out from the scientific community. And as time went on... he was forgotten. \\wHolly\\r: \nMadnar wasn't exactly happy with the scientific community, either. He must have been searching for some way to get back at them. \\wHolly\\r: \n...That's when Zanzibar Land talked him into becoming a double agent. \\wHolly\\r: \nHe'd use his status as a scientist to feed technological secrets from East and West to Zanzibar Land... \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nAnd, Dr. Marv's disappearance...? \\wHolly\\r: \nRight. The timing is too perfect. Madnar must have given them every detail of Marv's itinerary in the U.S. \\wSnake\\s: \nMadnar approached Marv and accompanied him to get OILIX from the very beginning. \\w" },
    { 5, 27, "en", "Holly\\r\\1: \nThanks, Snake, you saved me! \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n... \\wHolly\\r: \nWhat's wrong? \\wSnake\\s: \nI... didn't think you'd be this pretty. \\wHolly\\r: \nOh? Not what you pictured? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nI should have met up with you sooner. \\wHolly\\r: \nSnake, about Dr. Marv... I'm pretty sure he's OK. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nPretty sure? I thought you said you'd made contact. \\wHolly\\r: \nWell, I haven't actually met him. He's being held somewhere... But it seems he sent out a carrier pigeon. There should be \\wHolly\\r: \nsome kind of clue written on it. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nA pigeon? ...Where is it now? \\wHolly\\r: \nI found it, but it flew away just as I was about to catch it... It went up the elevator shaft in the tower building. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nToward the roof?! \\wHolly\\r: \nThey're searching for it desperately, too. We have to catch it first. It's our only clue to Dr. Marv's whereabouts. \\wSnake\\s: \nA pigeon hunt... What are you going to do? \\wHolly\\r: \nI'd only get in your way. I want to gather a little more info. My ratings have been slipping lately... And now this happens to me. \\wHolly\\r: \nI can't just let this go! \\wSnake\\s: \nThat's reassuring... Just don't push yourself too hard. \\wHolly\\r: \nThe enemy might be listening in, so let's change our frequency to 140.76. Ok, Snake? \\w" },
    { 5, 28, "en", "Snake\\s\\1: \nHolly?! \\wHolly\\r\\3: \nDid I scare you? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nWhew... that was a close one. So... what's going on? What are you doing here? \\wHolly\\r: \nYou said it yourself, remember? As long as we're alive, we can always meet again. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...So I did. \\wHolly\\r: \nUgh... that uniform was too tight in the chest... Ahh, I feel much better now. \\wHolly\\r: \nHere, I stole this gun from the enemy. You can have it. \\wSnake\\s: \nYeah... I can see how it'd be hard for a woman to use. Thanks. \\wHolly\\r: \n...So it's all over now. Right, Snake? \\wSnake\\s: \nNo... I still have one more job to do. \\wHolly\\r\\3: \n...You don't mean... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nThat's right... Holly? \\wHolly\\r\\1: \nSnake? You don't mean... me? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...Heh heh heh. ...Shall I call a car to pick us up? \\wHolly\\r\\1: \n...Oh... That was a harsh joke, Snake. \\w" },
    { 6, 0, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nBlack Color...He began making a name for himself about two years ago. Before that, his past is a blank. \\wKasler\\r: \nA high-tech ninja from NASA's extraterrestrial environment special forces unit. \\wKasler\\r: \nHis specialty is throwing stars and lightning-fast attacks. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe's not a professional soldier like us. He's an elite spaceman. \\wKasler\\r: \nThat's what makes him so hard to deal with. You can predict a professional's moves, but an amateur's another story. \\wKasler\\r: \nSnake, let's start by seeing what you've got... \\wKasler\\r: \nI'm counting on you, Lone Ranger! ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 1, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nRunning Man... He was a sprinter at the Barcelona Olympics. Ran the 100-meter dash in 9.69 seconds. \\wKasler\\r: \nThen he was expelled from the athletics association for doping, and got involved in terrorism in Europe. \\wKasler\\r: \nThere's no way you're gonna keep up with him. It's like a snake trying to catch a cheetah. You're gonna have to set a trap and catch \\wKasler\\r: \nhim. \\wKasler\\r: \nPlant a trap in his path and you might have a chance. \\wKasler\\r: \n...'Course, that's if you can do it before the gas gets there. The trick here is to use his speed against him...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 2, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nHind D... Just hearing that name is enough to make a grown man's blood run cold. \\wKasler\\r: \nHeh heh... Weight capacity 12,000 kg, top speed 250 kph, top altitude 4500 meters. \\wKasler\\r: \nIt's armed with missiles and a Vulcan cannon, and protected by titanium armor. A monster of the skies. \\wKasler\\r: \nIf it strafes you from above, you won't last a second. \\wKasler\\r: \nMeet one, and you've got no chance at all... at least, that's what I'd like to say. But stinger missiles have changed \\wKasler\\r: \nthings. \\wKasler\\r: \nWith stingers, you can bring down this monstrous bird...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 3, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nRed Blaster, huh? He's an elite assassin from the Soviet Union's Lumumba University known as the Red Bomber. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe'll set booby traps all around to pin his target down, then finish the job with his specialty - the grenade launcher. \\wKasler\\r: \nSnake, give him a taste of his own medicine! He's bound to be hiding behind a wall or something. \\wKasler\\r: \nA grenade can hit him even behind cover! ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 4, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nUltrabox, huh... An assassination squad assembled from former SAS, GSG9, and UDT, specializing in enclosed spaces. \\wKasler\\r: \nThey're all war professionals. They can kill without so much as blinking. Taking them all on at once puts you at a disadvantage. \\wKasler\\r: \nBest to take them down one at a time... Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 5, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nPredator... A former hunter from Rex Command. He's an expert in jungle guerilla combat. \\wKasler\\r: \nIn the jungle, he's almost beyond human. They say he wiped out two entire companies single-handed in Vietnam and South Yemen... \\wKasler\\r: \n ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 6, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nNight Sight? Snake, did you just say Night Sight?! You've made yourself one terrifying enemy. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe's a surviving member of the Whispers, a legendary guerilla unit. In North Vietnam they said he was better at jungle \\wKasler\\r: \nfighting than the Green Berets. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe's got the latest in camo technology - total stealth. Only a handful of people have ever laid eyes on him. \\wKasler\\r: \nAnd I'm not one of them! That's why they call him the Invisible Assassin. \\wKasler\\r: \nSnake, I think your luck might have just run out...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 7, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nGray Fox... Real name, Frank Jaeger. Former member of FOX HOUND. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe was the last man to hold the title of Fox in the Big Boss era. Decorated five times... \\wSnake\\s: \nYeah, I know exactly how good he is... As his junior, I know him better than anyone. \\wSnake\\s: \nHe's a cool-headed, composed hunter. He never lets his prey escape. Everybody in the unit respected him. Looked up to him. \\wKasler\\r: \nThat may be, Snake... but do you know about his past? It might help you out... \\wKasler\\r: \n10 years ago, we in the mercenary trade knew him as Hunter. Jaeger apparently means \"hunter\" in German. \\wKasler\\r: \nBack then, he was involved with some woman from the Eastern bloc. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe tried to get her to come over the fence, but it all fell through. \\wKasler\\r: \nApparently the West wasn't interested in taking her. That's when Frank started to resent the Western top brass. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nWhat was the woman's name?! \\wKasler\\r: \nShe was an Olympic skater. Name was Natasha Marcova... The kind of woman who sends a shiver down your spine. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nN... Natasha...Marcova?! \\wKasler\\r: \nSnake! If you manage to beat Fox... I'll tell everyone that Solid Snake is the greatest mercenary in the world. \\wKasler\\r: \n...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 6, 8, "en", "Kasler\\r: \nBig Boss... \\wKasler\\r: \nA legendary soldier alongside William Morgan. His very existence has become a myth among mercenaries. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nI already know all that! I need new information! \\wKasler\\r: \nOK, OK... but this is only a rumor, understand? Three years ago, when Outer Heaven fell, Big Boss was seriously wounded. \\wKasler\\r: \nHe almost died...\nHe lost both hands, both legs, his right eye, and his right ear. But somehow... he survived. \\wKasler\\r: \nThen an Eastern bloc despot took notice of what was left of him - a man reduced to an object. His talent as a soldier \\wKasler\\r: \nmust have been too good to pass up. \\wKasler\\r: \nThey fast-tracked Petrovich Madnar's Snatcher Project and made Big Boss its test subject. \\wKasler\\r: \nSome experiment called a \"cybernetics orgasm,\" or something like that. Point is, he's a man who isn't a man anymore. \\wKasler\\r: \nHard to believe, I know. \\wKasler\\r: \nIf it's true, Snake, you have no chance of winning. None of your special techniques will work on him. \\wKasler\\r: \nSnake... give it up... There's no way you can win this time...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 7, 0, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r: \\B14\\S99\nAh, I see you figured out my code... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nDr. Marv? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nIt's been a while. Eh, Solid Snake? \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nDr. Madnar? ...but how?! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nMarv and I often crossed paths at academic conferences in Prague. We didn't speak each other's language, but we were scientific \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \ncomrades, after a fashion. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI was captured along with Marv while traveling to America. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nAnd what about Dr. Marv?! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nHe was moved from here to the tower building a few days ago. It's a tall building a few kilometers north of here. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nDammit, too late again!\nSo Marv's in the tower building... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nSnake, can you guess why they've left me alive? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nThey must need you for something... and that means... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nYes... Metal Gear.\nSnake, it's here... In Zanzibar Land. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nThey've already completed a new Metal Gear. The one you destroyed three years ago was only a prototype... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nThe new, improved model has several times the power. They're also moving ahead with mass production of a lightweight version. \\wSnake\\s: \nThen it was Metal Gear that attacked the nuke disposal sites... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nPrecisely. Metal Gear is a nuclear-equipped walking tank. Its true power is unleashed only when it is armed with nuclear weapons. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nZanzibar Land now has the only nukes in the world. And they're after OILIX, an alternative energy source, as well. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nSnake... Now that you know all this, perhaps you can guess who is behind it...? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nBig... Boss?! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nThe very same! With Metal Gear and OILIX, he plots to rule the world. We cannot let them have OILIX! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nScience is not meant to be used only for killing. Marv's will is strong, but his heart is weak. We must hurry! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI don't know how long he can withstand their torture. \\wSnake\\s: \nIf they've used drugs on him, we're in trouble... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nMarv should have a microtransmitter inside his body, just like mine. The female STB agent escorting us gave them to us. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nIf you can find out the frequency, you can reach him on an ordinary radio. \\wSnake\\s: \nMadnar, what are you going to do? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nThe wall separating us is made of Chobham armor plate. You can't blast your way through it. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nJust leave me here and go rescue Marv, Snake. \\wSnake\\s: \nAll right. I'll come back for you later. \\wDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nSnake... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nMy daughter Ellen is a fan of yours. She just won't get married. It's becoming a problem... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \n...Oh, and I have a zoologist friend, Yozev Norden, who lives around here. You can reach him on frequency 140.40. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nHe should be able to help you with anything involving animals... \\wSnake\\s: \nDon't worry. I'll come back for you in time for your daughter's wedding. \\wDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nThank you, Snake... \\w \\B12" },
    { 7, 1, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r: \nMarv can only speak Czech and Slovak. He's also the wary type, and especially so in his current predicament. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nWhat about you, Madnar? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI can only speak Russian and English... Wait, I've got it! Natasha can speak to him! \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nNatasha? ...The STB woman who was escorting you? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nShe'll be able to understand him, and Marv should let his guard down around her. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nIs she safe, this woman? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNot to worry. Natasha is no ordinary woman. She is a professional agent. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nWhen we were captured, she alone managed to steal an enemy uniform and escape. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNo doubt she's hiding somewhere inside Zanzibar Land, waiting for her chance. \\wSnake\\s: \nDoes she have a radio? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNo, it was taken away right after we were captured... The only thing I know is that she's wearing an enemy uniform. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nSo there's nothing to go on... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nHere's your clue: she's a woman. Don't be fooled by her enemy disguise... There are no woman soldiers in this fortress. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nThat's your clue. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNatasha is a woman. Why not set up an ambush someplace that only a woman would go? Like the ladies' restroom... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nOver and out. \\w \\B08" },
    { 7, 2, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r: \nNatasha is a woman. Why not set up an ambush someplace that only a woman would go? Like the ladies' restroom...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 7, 3, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r: \nSnake, still no sign of Marv? ...They must be torturing him. Hurry and rescue him! ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 8, 0, "en", "Marv\\r: \nTady je Marv. Co m\303\241m d\304\233lat? Chceme jenom m\303\255r. \\wMarv\\r: \nD\304\233l\303\241me pouze sv\305\257j \303\272kol. Pevn\304\233 douf\303\241m, \305\276e m\304\233 zachr\303\241n\303\255te. M\305\257j p\305\231\303\255teli. \\wMarv\\r: \nDrah\303\275 p\305\231\303\255teli! \\wSnake\\r: \n...What's he saying...? I can't understand a word. Better ask Madnar. \\w" },
    { 8, 1, "en", "Natasha\\s: \nTady je Natasha. \\wMarv\\r: \nMarv. \\wNatasha\\s: \nPane doktore! Jak se c\303\255t\303\255te? \\wMarv\\r: \nD\304\233kuji. C\303\255t\303\255m se dob\305\231e. Natasha. Vypad\303\241te velmi dob\305\231e. \\wNatasha\\s: \nKde jste? Pane doktore? \\wMarv\\r: \nNa severu v\304\233\305\276\303\241k\305\257 je rozsedlina. Za n\303\255 maj\303\255 koncentr\303\241k. Tam jsem.  \\wNatasha\\s: \nUr\304\215it\304\233 V\303\241s zachr\303\241n\303\255me. \\wMarv\\r: \nJsem vd\304\233\304\215n\303\275. D\304\233kuji. \\w" },
    { 9, 6, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nYou should wait 30 minutes after eating before playing games. The blood flow shifts to your stomach, and your brain doesn't function as \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nquickly. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nThat's when your attention level is at its lowest. So you should wait 30 minutes after eating before you start playing...Over and \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nout. \\w" },
    { 9, 7, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nWhen replenishing your fluids, you shouldn't drink any more than 100 cc's at a time. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nWhen it absorbs fluids, your body burns an amount of energy equal to the temperature difference between your body and the fluid. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nThat's because it has to raise the fluid's temperature to match your body temperature. It also makes your blood thinner, slowing your \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nbrain functions. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nThat's why it's dangerous to play while drinking juice...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 8, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nYou can drink your own saliva, but never spit it out. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nThe enemy can tell how tired you are by looking at saliva on the ground or on plants. They can even estimate how long ago you were \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nthere. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nThat's why it's dangerous to spit on train station platforms...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 9, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nWhen it's time to act, act with total confidence - tell yourself, I can do this. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nHold on to the image of yourself succeeding. Even if you slip up, never picture yourself at the GAME OVER screen. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nEncourage yourself. Use the power of suggestion...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 11, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nWIS. OHIO... Only the H is lowercase? Hmm... I've got it! It's a digital number. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nYou see what I'm getting at, don't you, Snake? ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 12, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nWIS. OHIO... Try reading it upside down. They're not letters - they're numbers. You'll get Dr. Marv's frequency. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nBut watch that lowercase H. It was never a code at all - you were just looking at it upside down... \\wMaster Miller\\r: \n0140.51M...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 13, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nIt's an odd thing to say to a Snake, but snakes make for excellent food. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nTo eat a poisonous snake, cut off the head, take out the internal organs, peel off the skin, and grill the meat. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nSnakes are full of parasites, so you should cook them thoroughly before eating...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 15, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nHow to deal with concentrated sulfuric acid? Hmm, let's see... You could neutralize it if you had something with caustic soda in it... \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nI got it! ...You got any chocolate on you? That ought to do the trick. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nSulfuric acid reacts with the sugars in chocolate to produce carbon and a gummy residue. C12H22O11... a disaccharide. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nSee if you can find some chocolate...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 17, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nCheese, huh... You probably already know this, but the B3 ration has cheese in it. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nJust the thing to attract rats, don't you think? \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nUnrelated, but I know a place that makes a delicious cheese fondue... We should go eat there sometime...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 9, 18, "en", "Master Miller\\r: \nTo cure a sneeze, drink a full glass of water in seven sips, and then hold your breath for four seconds. It works surprisingly well. \\wMaster Miller\\r: \nIf it doesn't work, take some medicine...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 0, "en", "Norden\\r: \nWhy does FOX HOUND use animal names as code names, anyway? Thinking animals belong on a battlefield is pure human \\wNorden\\r: \narrogance. I just don't understand it...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 1, "en", "Norden\\r: \nThat's a wood pigeon, specially trained to act as a carrier pigeon. Did you know there are no fewer than 260 species of pigeon \\wNorden\\r: \nin the world? \\wNorden\\r: \nThey're about 40 centimeters long and are found from Europe all the way to South Asia. Dr. Marv probably brought that one with him. \\wNorden\\r: \nPigeons are timid, and very sensitive to noise. If you get too close, they'll sense you and fly away. Yet for all that, they're \\wNorden\\r: \nnotorious gluttons. \\wNorden\\r: \nThey feed mostly on grain... I got an idea!! If you have some beans or potatoes, you can use them as bait! \\wNorden\\r: \nI just got a large order of fries myself... Oh, right. Tough to find a burger stand out on the battlefield, eh? ...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 2, "en", "Norden\\r: \nFrom what you're telling me, I can't tell what kind of egg it is. Either a reptile egg or a bird egg... \\wNorden\\r: \nOh, that reminds me. With an egg in oden, the inside should still be white when you cut it open - but the broth has to have soaked \\wNorden\\r: \nall the way through...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 3, "en", "Norden\\r: \nThat's a Zanzibar wood owl. As I'm sure you know, owls are nocturnal hunters. There are about 120 species found throughout the \\wNorden\\r: \nworld. \\wNorden\\r: \nThe Zanzibar wood owl is about 20 centimeters long, and is found only in Central Asia. \\wNorden\\r: \nIt lays white eggs every 2 to 7 days. Incubation is carried out exclusively by the female. With genetic modifications, the eggs \\wNorden\\r: \ncan hatch in a few days. \\wNorden\\r: \nBecause that owl is nocturnal and because it always hoots right after sunset, people in Zanzibar Land use it to tell the time. \\wNorden\\r: \nIn fact, they trust it so much that once, when an owl hooted for some odd reason, they misread the call and mistook \\wNorden\\r: \nnight for day...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 4, "en", "Norden\\r: \nThat's probably a type of boa. It's nocturnal and has a gentle disposition. But it's a snake, and snakes love to eat. It'll eat just \\wNorden\\r: \nabout anything. \\wNorden\\r: \nI bet it'd love to eat your rations. Better get rid of it quick. Use the |6 button to let it go. \\wNorden\\r: \nWhen the snake reaches the egg's shell, let it go...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 10, 5, "en", "Norden\\r: \nProbably a Zanzibar hamster, said to be highly poisonous. There are 1,183 species of mice worldwide. \\wNorden\\r: \nHamsters are rodents, belonging to the mouse family. They grow to be about 25 to 28cm long, and are found from Western Europe \\wNorden\\r: \nthrough Siberia and into Iraq. \\wNorden\\r: \nThat variant was probably domesticated into a house mouse. House mice are very cautious creatures. They won't come out \\wNorden\\r: \nof their nests with humans around. \\wNorden\\r: \nTheir favorite food is cheese... That's it! Cheese! You can use cheese as bait! Do you have any on you? \\wNorden\\r: \nWhat a shame. I just ordered a pizza myself. Sorry...Over and out. \\w" },
    { 11, 0, "en", "Gray Fox\\r\\3: \nSnake! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nSnake! ...It's me, Gray Fox. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nFox! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nYou should have listened to my warnings, Snake. Now I'm afraid our friendship is at an end. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nThat elevator is going to be your tomb. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nWhat?! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nDo you hear that sound?\\S64 I've sent in an assassination team. They specialize in confined spaces...\\S64 \\wGray Fox\\r: \nBe sure to give them a proper welcome. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nThe ceiling---!! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nSnake, I'm glad I got to say goodbye...\\S64 Over and out. \\w" },
    { 11, 1, "en", "Gray Fox\\r: \nSnake...\nLooks like it's finally time for me to pass on the title of \"Fox\". \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nFox... why? \\wGray Fox\\r: \nI'm not like you, Snake... My situation is more... complicated. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nBig Boss might have been just another CO to you, but he saved my life - twice. This was way before I joined the unit. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nThe first time, I was a half-white living in Vietnam... Even after the war ended, half-whites were persecuted and forced into labor. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nHe saved me from that living hell. Just like he saved all the children here... \\wGray Fox\\r: \nThe second time was in Mozambique. I was being tortured as a RENAMO soldier, and he saved me again. They'd cut off my \\wGray Fox\\r: \nears and my nose... I was in terrible shape. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nAnd this is your idea of paying him back?! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nNo, you've got it wrong. I hate war. Just like all the kids here. But... I need it. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nMen of war like us can't live in ordinary society. We need the battlefield. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nBig Boss gives us a place to fight. Conflict is in our blood. We can't deny it. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nI was born on the battlefield... And I'll die on the battlefield. All we can do is fight, Snake... all we can do is fight. \\wGray Fox\\r: \nMaking people happy... making a woman happy... is something I could never do. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nYou mean... her? \\wGray Fox\\r: \nDying in action suits me. \\wSnake\\s: \nRest easy, Fox. I swear I won't turn out like you. \\wGray Fox\\r\\3: \nThose words... I'll take them with me to the next world...Good luck, Snake. ...Don't let your fans down. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nMy fans?! ...It was you, wasn't it? ...You were the voice on the radio! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nCall it the price of my selfishness... I'll go on ahead, Snake. \\wSnake\\s: \nYou won't be alone, Frank. Natasha's waiting for you on the other side. \\wGray Fox\\r\\3: \n...Natasha... \\wGray Fox\\r\\3: \n...Thank you... Snake... \\w" },
    { 11, 2, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nGray... Fox... \\wGray Fox\\r: \nThis bridge is closed!! I'm taking Madnar with me! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nHow about it, Snake? For old times' sake, I'm willing to look the other way - just this once. Get out of here! You hear me? \\wGray Fox\\r: \nGo back to your country - now! \\wGray Fox\\r: \nGot that, Snake?... Ha ha ha ha! \\w" },
    { 12, 0, "en", "Snake\\s: \nI came to get rid of the nightmares I've been having for the past three years. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nThe nightmares? They never go away, Snake. Taste the exhilaration and tension of combat just once, and you will spend the \\wBig Boss\\r: \nrest of your life on the battlefield. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nOnce your fighting instinct has surfaced... it never sleeps again. You crave ever stronger tension. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nThat uncontrollable feeling... As a mercenary, you should understand it. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nPower, money, even sex - none of it can satisfy your cravings. Only one thing can... WAR! \\wBig Boss\\r: \nAll I've done is give you a place for it. I've given you a reason to live. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nPlaying the saint now, Big Boss? \\wBig Boss\\r: \nYou saw those children, didn't you? Every one a victim of a war somewhere in the world. And every one a soldier in the making, \\wBig Boss\\r: \nready to carry the next war. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nStart a war, fan its flames, create victims... Then save them, train them... And feed them back onto the battlefield. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nIt's a perfectly logical system. In this world of ours, conflict never ends. And neither does our purpose... our raison d'etre. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nSo we'll never be out of work... Is that what you're saying? \\wBig Boss\\r: \nOn the battlefield, you and I are valuable commodities. But back \"home\", we're nothing but dead weight. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nThe only ones who'd come courting us would be journalists from some cheap tabloid - at best. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nYou and I are doomed to remain here until we die like dogs on the battlefield. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \n...I've only got one fight left. To free myself from your grip, to rid myself of these nightmares... Big Boss, I will defeat you! \\wBig Boss\\r: \nIt doesn't matter who wins here. Our fight will continue. The loser will be liberated from the battlefield, and the winner will remain. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nAnd the survivor will live out the rest of his days as a soldier. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nThere are exceptions. I... love life. \\wBig Boss\\r: \nVery well, Snake. I'll release you from your suffering. As your former commander, I'll do you one last favor... and put you out of your \\wBig Boss\\r: \nmisery. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nI don't need any more favors from you! \\wBig Boss\\r: \nReally?...\nAnd just how do you expect to beat me in your condition? With no weapon? \\wSnake\\s: \nNever give up, right until the end. No matter how desperate the situation, picture yourself succeeding.\n\\wSnake\\s: \n ...Those are your words. \\wBig Boss\\r\\1: \nEven I make mistakes from time to time. \\wBig Boss\\r\\1: \nSnake!\nThis time, our final battle... One chance only... Come on!! \\w" },
    { 13, 0, "en", "Natasha\\r: \n...Yes, that's me... I am Natasha Marcova of the STB. \\wNatasha\\r: \nAnd you must be Solid Snake... We're after the same thing. Why don't we work together to save Dr. Marv? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...Have we met somewhere before? \\wNatasha\\r: \nIsn't that a typical pick-up line from Western men? \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nNow I remember! You're Natasha Marcova, the Ice Fairy. You took the gold at the Calgary Olympics. \\wNatasha\\r\\1: \n...You must be mistaken. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nI don't think so. I know I've... \\wNatasha\\r: \nMore importantly - what about Dr. Marv? \\wSnake\\s: \nI made contact with him over the radio, but we couldn't understand each other. \\wNatasha\\r: \nThen he's safe... Good. I'm glad he had that surgery to implant the microtransmitter. Snake, lend me your radio... \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nThe frequency is 140.51. \\w" },
    { 13, 1, "en", "Natasha\\r\\3: \n...How odd... \\wSnake\\s: \nCan't be helped. Madnar may not look it, but he's an old man. \\wNatasha\\r: \nNo, I mean us... A world-famous genius scientist, a former Olympic athlete, and an ex-special forces soldier, all down in a sewer... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...That's fate. \\wNatasha\\r: \nFate? Yes... perhaps you're right...You know, when I was a little girl, my mother used to tell me stories. \\wNatasha\\r: \nAbout Poland during World War II... about the Warsaw uprising. My mother spent days in the sewers under the city fleeing from the \\wNatasha\\r: \nNazis. \\wNatasha\\r: \nShe was black with mud... You could hardly recognize her face... My mother and I are much alike. We are both \\wNatasha\\r: \nhaunted by war. \\wSnake\\s: \n...Natasha, why'd you quit skating and join STB? You'd think an Olympic athlete would be treated well, even in the East. \\wNatasha\\r\\3:  \n...Not exactly. It was something about the ice... It felt... cold. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nThe ice...? \\wNatasha\\r: \nSnake, are you married? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...No, I don't have a family. You? \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nI'm all alone... And it's not because I like being single, either. Perhaps I simply never had the chance. \\wSnake\\s: \nWhat about a boyfriend? \\wNatasha\\r: \n...Once... only once... I thought about getting married. It was back when I was still skating. \\wNatasha\\r: \nI was deeply, madly in love... It still hurts to think about it. He was a Western man. His name was Frank Hunter. \\wNatasha\\r: \nHe was handsome, well-mannered, intelligent... But always afraid of something. \\wNatasha\\r: \nI would have thrown it all away for him. My family, skating, everything... I would have followed him anywhere. \\wSnake\\s: \nYou would have defected? \\wNatasha\\r: \nYes... But it was not to be. The West rejected my bid for asylum at the last minute. Some sort of political reasons... I still don't \\wNatasha\\r: \nunderstand. \\wSnake\\s: \nThe reception committee just wasn't ready for you. It happens a lot. \\wNatasha\\r: \nEver since, my family and I have had a hard life... We lost our right to compete, were branded as refuseniks... I had no choice but to \\wNatasha\\r: \ngo into STB. \\wNatasha\\r: \nBut I have no regrets. When I was on the ice, I knew only the ice. Now I know so much more... I've even killed someone. \\wSnake\\s: \nWhat about him? Did you ever...? \\wNatasha\\r: \nI never saw him again... The Berlin Wall within us remained forever. \\wDr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nHello again! Sorry to keep you waiting. \\w" },
    { 13, 2, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \n...Na... Natasha... \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \n...Ah... I... \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nIt seems... I really could only ever walk on the ice... \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nI was always skating around... I never learned to plant my two feet on the ground and walk... \\wSnake\\s: \nThe ice between East and West is beginning to melt. Natasha... this time, plant your feet firmly on the ground. \\wSnake\\s: \nIt's time to stand firm in your own life, and savor it. \\wSnake\\s: \nNatasha? Not yet... Not yet... \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nIt's all right... I've watched many people die. I know... exactly what state I'm in. \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \n...It's a shame. Just when I'd met someone wonderful again... \\wSnake\\s: \nI would have liked to see you skate again. \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nTh... thank you... Take this... card 6. It opens the door. And this... my brooch. To use it, you... \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nHow? How do I use it? \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nI... can't... hold on... \\wNatasha\\r: \\f\\3\n...Frank... \\W \\W \\WDr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nSnake!! \\w" },
    { 14, 6, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nHuh...? \nThere's a piece of paper tied to the pigeon's leg. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nHELP! WIS. 0hI0\nKIO MARV... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nOnly the H is in lowercase... Some kind of message from Dr. Marv? What could it mean? \\w" },
    { 14, 7, "en", "Is it that late already?" },
    { 14, 13, "en", "He doesn't seem to be here." },
    { 15, 2, "en", "Kid\\r: \nI heard this ditch is connected to the next building by a jet of water. \\w" },
    { 15, 3, "en", "Kid\\r: \nThe one-eyed man told us that if a man in green came by, we should tell him the lady isn't here. \\w" },
    { 15, 4, "en", "Kid\\r\\3: \nDid you know? There's an old sewer under the ditch. \\w" },
    { 15, 5, "en", "Kid\\r: \nThe one-eyed man said we shouldn't go against the current. \\wKid\\r: \nHe said if you give yourself to the current, you'll see things you couldn't see before... Do you know what he meant? \\w" },
    { 15, 6, "en", "Kid\\r: \nThere's an animal pen northwest of here. \\w" },
    { 15, 7, "en", "Kid\\r: \nKnow what? At night, this place runs on its own generators. So the laser fences that need power get shut off. \\wKid\\r: \nThen we get to play inside, as long as the grown-ups don't catch us. \\w" },
    { 15, 13, "en", "Kid\\r: \nGive me chocolate! Mister, you got a B1 ration? \\wKid\\r: \nB1 rations have chocolate in them. \\w" },
    { 15, 14, "en", "Kid\\r: \nThere's lots of rats in the jail. They steal all kinds of things and take them back to their nests. \\wKid\\r: \nThe grown-ups put out concentrated sulfuric acid to try and get rid of them. \\w" },
    { 15, 18, "en", "Kid\\r\\1: \nI hate people carrying guns! \\w" },
    { 15, 19, "en", "Kid\\r: \nWanna know a secret? \\wKid\\r: \nYou know Natasha's brooch? It changes shape when you put it in the sauna or the freezer. \\w" },
    { 15, 21, "en", "Kid\\r: \nNatasha's locker is the one in the upper row, all the way to the right. I saw her there a lot when she came out of the sauna. \\w" },
    { 15, 23, "en", "Kid\\r: \nThe grown-ups always stand at attention when they hear the national anthem. That's the rule, apparently. \\w" },
    { 17, 0, "en", "It is the late 1990s... The\nworld is about to enter an age\nof stability." },
    { 17, 1, "en", "As U.S.-Soviet and Sino-Soviet\nrelations thaw, regional\nconflicts move toward\nreconciliation. The nuclear\nthreat that plagued this\ncentury is becoming a thing of\nthe past." },
    { 17, 5, "en", "Zanzibar Land attacks nuclear\nweapons disposal sites around the\nworld, seizing those weapons that\nare still intact, and becomes the\nworld's only nuclear power. It\nthen begins indiscriminately\ninvading its neighbors." },
    { 17, 6, "en", "After renouncing nuclear weapons,\nthe world is once again threatened\nby the specter of nuclear war." },
    { 17, 7, "en", "Meanwhile, the Earth's oil\nresources, said to be sufficient\nfor another 30 years, are running\nout sooner than expected. With no\nsafe alternative energy source,\nthe world faces a severe energy\ncrisis." },
    { 17, 8, "en", "It is in these dire circumstances\nthat Dr. Kio Marv, a Czech\nbiologist, develops \"OILIX\", a\nmicrobe that can produce\nhigh-purity petroleum." },
    { 17, 9, "en", "Tensions rise again over OILIX.\nKio Marv sets out for a\nscientific conference in\nAmerica, but Zanzibar Land\nabducts him on the way." },
    { 17, 10, "en", "With its nuclear weapons and\nOILIX, Zanzibar Land plans to\nachieve military superiority." },
    { 17, 11, "en", "A tiny microbe, only a few\nmicrons wide, is about to change\nthe world." },
    { 19, 0, "en", "Marv\\r\\3: \nHeh heh heh... Foolish FOX HOUNDER! \\wMarv\\r: \nDr. Marv isn't here! Fooled by a cheap transmitter like this? FOX HOUND really is behind the times. \\w" },
    { 19, 1, "en", "Black Color\\r: \nI am Black Color, a former member of NASA's extraterrestrial environment special forces unit. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nNow, let's see what this so-called FOX HOUND can really do - the world's foremost high-tech irregular warfare unit! \\wBlack Color\\r: \nShow me what you've got, FOX HOUNDER! \\w" },
    { 19, 2, "en", "Black Color\\r\\3: \n...Snake... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nWho are you? ...How do you know my name? \\wBlack Color\\r: \nIt's... it's me... Schneider. Kyle Schneider. Remember me? \\wSnake\\s: \nSchneider? ...You were in the Resistance at Outer Heaven! \\wSnake\\s: \nBut... I thought they killed you! \\wBlack Color\\r: \nYou've still got a lot to learn, Snake. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nI was almost killed, but not by them. By you, and your country. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nWhat are you saying, Schneider? \\wBlack Color\\r: \n...Snake, after you destroyed Metal Gear, \\wBlack Color\\r: \nNATO launched a massive bombing campaign against Outer Heaven. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nAll of us in the Resistance... and the women and children of Outer Heaven... we were all abandoned.\n \\wBlack Color\\r: \nThey ran through the raging flames... and died where they fell. \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nI... can't believe this... \\wBlack Color\\r: \nThink about it. The children of Outer Heaven were originally war orphans and refugees from all over the world. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nTo them, children like that were something they'd rather not touch... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \n...No... \\wBlack Color\\r: \nYou're no different. They'll forget about you, too... But that man... \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nThat man...? \\wBlack Color\\r: \nThe one who saved us as we fled... was that man. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nThat man forgave us for what we'd done, and gave us a new land, a new family... \\wSnake\\s: \nThat man... You can't mean... \\wBlack Color\\r: \nSnake, soon you too will understand... how wonderful that man is... \\wBlack Color\\r: \nSnake... I owe you a debt. There's no hate between us. I'll tell you where the doctor is. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nIt won't go against his wishes... Find the man guarding the cell where the doctor is being held. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nFollow that man...and you'll reach the cell. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nYou can tell him by his green beret. He should be on the first floor. Got that? A green beret. \\wBlack Color\\r: \nFollow the man in the green beret! \\w" },
    { 19, 3, "en", "Running Man\\r: \nA visitor at last! ...You've come at just the right time. \\wRunning Man\\r: \nI was about to go for a little run. \\wRunning Man\\r: \nI am Running Man, the world's fastest mercenary. Think you can keep up with me? \\wRunning Man\\r\\1: \nSee for yourself!! \\w" },
    { 19, 4, "en", "Running Man\\r\\3: \n...pant...pant... What do you think? Pretty fast, eh? Time to get serious! \\wRunning Man\\r: \nHear that sound?\\S64 That's nerve gas.\\S64 Defeat me before the gas gets to you, and you'll survive.\\S64 \\wRunning Man\\r: \nThe clock is ticking... Let the race begin! \\w" },
    { 19, 5, "en", "Running Man\\r\\3: \n...You... you used my speed against me... What's your name? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nSnake... Solid Snake. \\wRunning Man\\r: \n...Snake....? The cheetah has lost to a snake...? How could this happen? \\wSnake\\s: \n...Guess you were in a hurry to die. \\w" },
    { 19, 6, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nWh... What is this? ...A booby trap? \\wRed Blaster\\r: \nThat's right. A trap for taking a fox alive - FOX HOUNDER! \\w" },
    { 19, 7, "en", "Red Blaster\\r: \nI am Red Blaster, and you're not going anywhere. I'll take my time cooking you with my grenades. \\w" },
    { 19, 8, "en", "Ultrabox\\r: \nWe are Ultrabox, an assassination squad specializing in confined spaces. \\wUltrabox\\r: \nWe are the President's own top-secret team. \\wUltrabox\\r: \nConsider it an honor to be cooked by us. \\w" },
    { 19, 9, "en", "Predator\\r: \nI've been waiting for you, Snake! I am Predator, the undisputed master of the jungle ambush. \\wPredator\\r: \nLet's see whether you're a real snake or not! \\w" },
    { 19, 10, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r: \nAh! ...Snake, you're too late. He died just now. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nHis heart couldn't take it anymore. \\w" },
    { 19, 11, "en", "Snake\\s: \nWait... what's that bruise on his neck?! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNot to worry, Snake. Marv may be dead, but the plans for OILIX are safe. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nMarv was a very careful man. He left the plans behind, in case anything should happen. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nHe had a reputation as a video game enthusiast. He even used to have them shipped to him from the West every month. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nA few days ago, it seems he hid some microfilm in the circuit board of one of his game cartridges. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nApparently it was an MSX cartridge, made by a Japanese game company called Konami. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nMSX... That's the world's best-selling brand of computer, isn't it? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nAnd it seems he put that cartridge inside the locker over there. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nWhere's the key? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI don't have it... He wouldn't talk. No... he never told me anything! \\w" },
    { 19, 12, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nThat's about the size of it, Snake. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI staked everything on your world... For that, I left the country I had called home... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nBut you people slandered me, and condemned everything I did. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI just wanted... to finish Metal Gear! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nTo pour everything I know of robotology into it! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nBut your politicians were only interested in nonsense like SDI, NEDW, and brain bombs! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI kept passing on scientific information from East and West... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nAnd with their support, I continued improving Metal Gear. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nMadnar, did you kill Dr. Marv? \\wDr. Madnar\\r\\1: \n...Yes! Because he refused to hand over the OILIX plans! \\wDr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nAnd it was I who caused Natasha's death on the bridge by contacting Fox from the sewer! \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nThe bathroom break...! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nSnake, I know Marv - no, Natasha - gave you the key to the locker! Give it to me!! \\w" },
    { 19, 13, "en", "Gray Fox\\r\\1: \nSnake...I'm not the same as I used to be. And neither is Metal Gear. \\wGray Fox\\r\\1: \nI'll make you taste real fear... and the true feeling of defeat! \\w" },
    { 19, 14, "en", "Gray Fox\\r\\1: \nThe cartridge is mine, Snake! ...Now burn to death! \\w" },
    { 19, 15, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nWhere am I? \\wGray Fox\\r: \nIsn't this the perfect ring to settle things? \\w" },
    { 19, 16, "en", "Gray Fox\\r: \nIt's been a while, Snake... Here in this minefield... What say we go at it hand to hand! \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nA chicken fight? \\wGray Fox\\r: \nThe two greatest rivals in FOX HOUND... I've been waiting for this moment for a long time. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nFox!\nI'll beat some sense back into you! \\wGray Fox\\r\\1: \nSnake!\nI'll show you what the title of Fox is worth! \\w" },
    { 19, 17, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nBig Boss... you're alive?! \\wBig Boss\\r: \nSnake...\nWelcome to Zanzibar Land... So you've come back to me after all. \\w" },
    { 19, 20, "en", "Not yet... Not yet..." },
    { 19, 21, "en", "Not yet... Not yet..." },
    { 19, 22, "en", "Snake... Sna..." },
    { 19, 25, "en", "All right, go ahead!" },
    { 20, 1, "en", "Gray Fox\\r\\1: \nSnake! There's no way to destroy this Metal Gear. That's just a washed-up old scientist's wishful thinking! \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nFox!! ...Where are you? \\wGray Fox\\r\\3: \nWe'll meet soon, Snake. Go through the front door! \\w" },
    { 20, 2, "en", "Holly\\r: \nOh, and I made a copy of my card. It's card 4. Use it... \\wHolly\\r: \nSee you, Snake... Catch you later. \\w" },
    { 20, 4, "en", "Holly\\r\\3: \nWhat...? \\wSnake\\s: \nThat's the kind of thing lovers say when they part. \\wHolly\\r: \n...Then what are we, Snake? ...What should I say? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nAs long as we're alive, we can always meet again... \\wHolly\\r\\3: \n...All right. \\w" },
    { 20, 5, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nNatasha? \\w" },
    { 20, 6, "en", "Natasha\\r: \nSnake, Dr. Marv is safe... for now. There's a large crevice north of the tower building. It seems he's being held in the \\wNatasha\\r: \nprison on the far side. \\wNatasha\\r: \nDr. Marv also expressed concern about Dr. Madnar. \\wSnake\\s: \nMadnar is safe. Don't worry. We rescue Marv first... Got it? \\w" },
    { 20, 7, "en", "Natasha\\r: \nI know a shortcut to the crevice. There's an old sewer running under here. We can take that elevator down. Let's go. \\w" },
    { 20, 9, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nOh! ...Natasha! Snake! \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nDoctor, you're all right! \\wSnake\\s: \n...You've lost some weight, Madnar... \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nAnd you haven't changed a bit, Snake. \\wNatasha\\r\\1: \nSnake, we must hurry! We have to get to Dr. Marv! \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nWhat? Marv is safe? \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI tried to find a way out of here myself, but this elevator won't open from the inside. \\wSnake\\s\\1: \nNatasha - we move out single file. Stay behind me. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nNo, wait! Snake, I have something to give you. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nI swiped it from a guard... It's card 5. \\wNatasha\\r: \nLead the way, Snake. I'll follow you. \\w" },
    { 20, 10, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nSnake, wait! I can't go on... I must rest a little... \\wNatasha\\r\\3: \nSnake...? \\wSnake\\s\\3: \nAll right... we'll take a short break. \\wDr. Madnar\\r: \nPlease excuse me. I... have some business to take care of. \\w" },
    { 20, 11, "en", "Snake\\s\\3: \nThat was some bathroom break. \\wNatasha\\r\\1: \n...Let's go, Snake. \\w" },
    { 20, 12, "en", "Snake\\s\\1: \nA bridge!! \\WNatasha\\r: \nWe can only cross it one at a time. \\WDr. Madnar\\r: \nI'll go first. I haven't got long left anyway. Whatever happens, no one will grieve for me. \\W" },
    { 20, 13, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r\\1: \nIt's all right! You can come across! \\WNatasha\\r: \nOK, I'm next... I'll go on ahead, Snake. \\W" },
    { 20, 14, "en", "Natasha\\r: \nIt looks safe, Snake! Hurry and cross over! \\W" },
    { 20, 15, "en", "Snake\\s\\1: \nNatasha!! \\w" },
    { 20, 18, "en", "Snake\\s: \nFox! I won't give up! \\w" },
    { 20, 19, "en", "Holly\\r: \n...Sorry. It's OK... It's me. \\w" },
    { 20, 20, "en", "Snake\\s: \nHolly, we've got to run as fast as we can to the rendezvous point. Think you can keep up? \\wHolly\\r\\3: \n...Was that a proposal, Snake? \\wSnake\\s: \nJudging by that response, you'll be fine. \\w" },
    { 20, 23, "en", "Snake\\s: \nThink we'll make it back in time for Christmas? \\WHolly\\r: \nThere's still time for dinner, Snake. \\WSnake\\s: \nLet's go, then...\nChrist isn't going anywhere. \\W" },
    { 20, 24, "en", "Dr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nSnake... he'll never let you get away. \\WDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nHe'll use it... he'll use Metal Gear. \\WDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nA present... for my daughter Ellen... \\WDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nI'll tell you... how to destroy it. \\WSnake\\s: \nHow to destroy the new Metal Gear? \\WDr. Madnar\\r: \nI could never cross the wall between East and West... the one inside my own heart. \\WDr. Madnar\\r: \nBut my daughter is different. Snake... for Ellen, the daughter I left behind in the East... \\WSnake\\s\\1: \nHow do I destroy Metal Gear? \\WDr. Madnar\\r\\3: \nThe leg armor is thin... Use grenades on the legs. It is the only way... \\W" },
    { 20, 25, "en", "Campbell\\r: \nGood work, Snake. Have you thought about... coming back to the unit? \\WSnake\\s: \n...The nightmares have stopped. I'm a free man now. \\WCampbell\\r: \nI see... that's too bad. By the way, about that cartridge... Is it really the one Dr. Marv left behind? \\WHolly\\r: \nWhy don't we open it and find out? \\WSnake\\s: \nNo need for that. The cartridge I brought back is the one Dr. Marv left behind, no question. Just put it straight in the MSX. \\WCampbell\\r: \nAll right... here goes. \\W" },
    { 20, 26, "en", "Holly\\r: \n...Huh? ...Nothing's happening. \\WCampbell\\r: \nWhat on earth... Of course! Snake was right! No doubt about it - this is the cartridge Dr. Marv left behind! \\WHolly\\r: \nWhat are you talking about? ...I don't see anything. \\WSnake\\s: \nHere, look closer... Dr. Marv signed it... Right here. His full name - \"KIO MARV.\" \\WHolly\\r: \nI see it now! ...It's upside down. \\WCampbell\\r: \nThis will save the world... \\WSnake\\s: \nDr. Marv's last performance. \\WHolly\\r: \nHe really loved games, didn't he? From the bottom of his heart. \\WCampbell\\r: \nDr. Marv was entangled in an absurd political game... and it cost him his life. \\WHolly\\r: \nBut... the game he left behind saved us all. Right, Snake? \\WHolly\\r\\1: \nSnake? ...Where'd he go? Hey, Snake's gone! \\WCampbell\\r: \n...Snake? ...Gave us the slip, did he? \\WHolly\\r\\1: \nSnake! SNAKE! ...And after we promised to have dinner... That's just mean! \\W" },
    { 22, 7, "en", "Norden" },
    { 22, 8, "en", "One of your fans" },
    { 23, 11, "en", "BLACK COLOR" },
    { 23, 14, "en", "ULTRABOX" },
    { 23, 15, "en", "NIGHT SIGHT" },
} };
